[b]Tertium 5 note:[/b] Tertium 5 can crash on Arbites and Hive Scum profiles. Use [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/warhammer40kdarktide/mods/725]Tertium 6[/url] if you want all current classes.

[size=3][b]Common questions[/b][/size]

[b]Does this work in public matches, public Havoc, or private duo?[/b]
No. Those bots run on Fatshark's dedicated servers, even when the lobby is private or starts with empty slots. BetterBots needs a locally hosted Solo Play mission.

[b]Does this add rewards or progression to Solo Play?[/b]
No. BetterBots changes bot behavior. Rewards, progression, and backend access are separate from this mod.

[b]Do I need multiple leveled characters?[/b]
No. BetterBots ships bot-optimized profiles for the original classes, and Tertium 6 can use your own characters as bots if you prefer that setup.

[b]Can I get multiple built-in loadouts per class?[/b]
Not through the in-game UI right now. Manual profile editing is documented, but a proper profile manager is future-work territory.

[size=3][b]Install[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Extract [font=Courier New]BetterBots.zip[/font] into your Darktide [font=Courier New]mods/[/font] folder.
[*]Add [font=Courier New]BetterBots[/font] to [font=Courier New]mods/mod_load_order.txt[/font] below [font=Courier New]dmf[/font].
[*]Re-patch mods.
[*]Start a Solo Play mission and check for [font=Courier New]BetterBots loaded[/font] in chat.
[/list]

Darktide disables mods after game updates. If the mod suddenly stops loading after a patch, re-run the mod toggle/patch script first.

[size=3][b]Known limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Hive Scum support is implemented but not validated by me in-game because I do not own the DLC. Reports are useful.
[*]Item-style abilities such as Zealot relic, Psyker Force Field, Arbites Cyber-Mastiff, and Hive Scum Stimm Supply use wield/use/unwield sequences. Darktide patches can break those paths until the mod is updated.
[*]Bots are still bots. They do not animation-cancel, dodge, aim, or manage risk like a strong human player. The goal is better Solo Play support, not human-level play.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Bug reports and source[/b][/size]

If something breaks, the most useful report is: what happened, your bot lineup, whether you were in Solo Play, and the relevant [font=Courier New]bb-log summary[/font] / [font=Courier New]bb-log warnings[/font] output if you can grab it.

